---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Projects | Sam's Portfolio"
	description="A showcase of my personal and professional projects - coming soon."
	keywords={["projects", "portfolio", "software development", "web development"]}
>
	<section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24 flex flex-col items-center justify-center text-center">
		<h1 class="font-teko text-5xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-foreground sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl mb-6">Projects</h1>
		<p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-8">Coming Soon</p>
		<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
			<p>
				While I don't have demonstrable projects to showcase just yet, it's not for lack of passion for technology.
			</p>
			<p>
				Life has been wonderfully busy lately. My family welcomed our second child in June 2025, and we moved into a new house in December 2024 that's been keeping me occupied with renovations.
			</p>
			<p>
				So instead of tinkering with the tech I love, I've been building out my DIY skills, one project at a time, just in a different domain!
			</p>
			<p class="pt-4 text-foreground font-medium">
				Check back soon for updates.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
